course: dictionary
lesson: 2893
title: Double: one word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word double can do different jobs in a sentence. As a verb, to double means to make something two times as much or as many: «doubling in a loop grows fast: 10, 20, 40, 80.»
explain: As an adjective, double means two of the same, or twice the size: «a double bed», «double letters». As a noun, a double is a person who looks just like someone else.
explain: Read the words around double to find its job. In «a double bed», double describes the bed, so it is an adjective. When double follows a person or thing that does something, as in «The rain doubled overnight», it is a verb.
fact: To double means to make or become two times as many or as much.
fact: Double as an adjective means two of the same, or twice the size.
fact: Doubles facts such as 6 + 6 = 12 help you add quickly.
fact: In spelling, double letters like «ll» in «ball» are two of the same letter in a row.
fact: Longer words double their last letter only when the beat falls on the last part: «be-GIN», beginning; «for-GET», forgetting.
exercise: «Doubling in a loop grows fast: 10, 20, 40, 80.» In this sentence, what does doubling mean? | *Making each number two times as big as the one before | Stopping after one turn | Adding the same small number each time | Writing the numbers backwards
exercise: Connor looks up «a double-double». What is it? | *Coffee with two creams and two sugars | A game with two dice | A type of dog | A woolly hat
exercise: A doubles fact like 7 + 7 helps you add. What is 7 + 7? | *14 | 12 | 16 | 13
test: In «a double bed», what kind of word is double? | A verb | A noun | A letter | *An adjective
test: Which word doubles its last letter when you add -ing, because the beat falls on the last part? | visit | *begin | open | jump
exam: Which sentence uses double as a noun, meaning a person who looks just like someone else? | *Ben's cousin is his double, they look exactly the same. | Please double-check your sums before you hand them in. | Mia has a double bed in her room. | Dad will double the recipe for the party.
